        "original_id": "e205e283-4c19-5615-9a2e-853d182ff08f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Melville, Hamilton, New Zealand\n- People: James Dougal Melville, Douglas Bader, Paul Brickhill\n- Roles: Royal Air Force flying ace, aviator\n- Works: Reach for the Sky, Reach for the Sky biography\n\nFacts:\n- Melville is a suburb in southern Hamilton in New Zealand.\n- Melville is named after James Dougal Melville.\n- Douglas Bader was born on 21 February 1910 and died on 5 September 1982.\n- Douglas Bader was a Royal Air Force flying ace during the Second World War.\n- Paul Brickhill wrote the 1954 biography Reach for the Sky about Douglas Bader.\n- Reach for the Sky is a 1956 British biographical film about Douglas Bader.\n- The 1956 film Reach for the Sky was based on Paul Brickhill’s 1954 biography of the same name.",
